      "dataset": "Harmonized Landsat Sentinel-2 (HLS) v2.0, L30 and S30 surface reflectance and Fmask",
      "provider": "NASA LP DAAC (Ju et al. 2025, doi:10.1016/j.rse.2025.114723), served by Microsoft Planetary Computer",
      "spatial_resolution": "30 m",
      "temporal_coverage": "2020–2025, every 2–3 days before clouds",
      "access_url": "https://planetarycomputer.microsoft.com/dataset/hls2-l30",
      "note": "The 30 m pixel containing the field centre. NDVI = (NIR − red)/(NIR + red) from nadir BRDF-adjusted reflectance: Landsat 8/9 bands B05 and B04, Sentinel-2 bands B8A and B04, bandpass-adjusted to Landsat by HLS. An observation is clear when Fmask bits 1–5 (cloud, adjacent to cloud or shadow, cloud shadow, snow/ice, water) are all 0 and the aerosol level is not high (HLS v2.0 user guide, Table 9). Scenes with more than 80 % cloud over the tile are not read; overlapping tiles are counted once per date. Season = April–September, with a mean only when at least 5 observations are clear."
